---
/**
 * Who makes Sukhi Play: one parent, for his own children.
 *
 * A page a parent reads before trusting a stranger's software with their
 * child's screen, and the page search engines and assistants use to answer
 * "who is behind this". Marked up as a ProfilePage for the Person every post
 * is written by, so the blog's author has somewhere to point.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Img from '../components/Img.astro';
import { AUTHOR, longDate, posts } from '../blog';
import { REPO, SITE } from '../site';

const news = (await posts()).filter((p) => p.data.kind !== 'guide').reverse();

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ProfilePage',
  url: `${SITE}/about/`,
  name: 'Who makes Sukhi Play',
  mainEntity: {
    ...AUTHOR,
    description: 'A parent who builds Sukhi Play, a free locked-down browser for small children, and the playground apps for his own son and daughter.',
    knowsAbout: ['kiosk browsers for children', 'screen time for toddlers', 'Electron', 'web apps for children']
  },
  about: { '@type': 'SoftwareApplication', name: 'Sukhi Play', url: SITE }
};
---

<Base
  title="Who makes Sukhi Play"
  description="Sukhi Play is made by Mandeep Singh, a parent, for his own children. No company, no investors, no adverts: one person, and every line of code public."
  page="about"
  schema={schema}>

  <main class="wrap whois">
    <header class="whois-hero">
      <Img src="/assets/mandeep.png" alt="Mandeep Singh, drawn in the same style as Sukhi and Jazz, smiling with his arms folded" width="180" height="180" loading="eager" sizes="180px" />
      <div>
        <p class="f-kicker">Who makes it</p>
        <h1>One parent, making things for his children</h1>
        <p class="lede">I am Mandeep Singh. I built Sukhi Play for my son, and I
          keep making things for him and his sister. Other families are welcome to
          everything.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="whois-facts" aria-label="In short">
      <div><b>No company</b><span>One person. No investors, no staff, nothing to sell.</span></div>
      <div><b>No adverts</b><span>Not in the app, not in the playground, not on this site.</span></div>
      <div><b>Nothing collected</b><span>No account. The app sends nothing about your child anywhere.</span></div>
      <div><b>Code in public</b><span>Every line, including what decides what a child can reach.</span></div>
    </section>

    <div class="whois-body doc-body">
      <h2>Why it exists</h2>
      <p>My son Sukhraj, Sukhi to everyone, was three and wanted to play games on
        my laptop. He also pressed every key and clicked every button he could
        reach, which meant adverts, popups, new tabs, and eventually my work.</p>
      <p>I wanted to hand him the laptop and stop watching over his shoulder. So I
        built a screen where pressing every key is perfectly safe: the sites I
        chose, as big tiles, and nothing else. That became
        <a href="/blog/sukhi-play-1-0/">Sukhi Play 1.0</a>.</p>

      <h2>What it grew into</h2>
      <p>His sister Jazz is ten and loves stationery, so she got
        <a href="/studio/">Jazz's Studio</a>. Sukhi got <a href="/colouring/">a
        colouring book</a> of his own, and now <a href="/playground/#experiments">a
        railway</a> I am still testing with him. The studio and the colouring book work
        in any browser and inside Sukhi Play, with no internet; the railway stays on
        the website until children show they love it.</p>

      <h2>How to reach me</h2>
      <p>The best way is <a href={`${REPO}/issues`}>an issue on GitHub</a>: a bug,
        a site that does not work, or how an experiment went with your child.
        There is more about me at <a href="https://www.msingh.com">msingh.com</a>.</p>
    </div>

    {news.length > 0 && (
      <section class="whois-story" aria-labelledby="story-head">
        <h2 id="story-head">So far</h2>
        <ol class="whois-line">
          {news.map((p) => (
            <li>
              <time datetime={p.data.date.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}>{longDate(p.data.date)}</time>
              <a href={`/blog/${p.id}/`}>{p.data.title}</a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </section>
    )}
  </main>
</Base>
